{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJmk3EBndMEaBJfbYW8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015HoHDDgpPS9NdAfJVLrCRY","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-3wd0Ky/memory/api-dates-are-calendar-dates.md","content":"---\nname: api-dates-are-calendar-dates\ndescription: API response bodies must return dates as calendar-date strings (e.g. 2026-03-31), never full timestamps; GET /invoices issuedOn is a known exception pending migration\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nAgreement with the mobile team: any date in an API response body is a calendar date string such as `2026-03-31`, never a full timestamp.\n\n**Why:** The mobile app rendered full timestamps in the user's time zone, so customers west of UTC saw the previous day.\n\n**How to apply:** When adding or changing response fields that hold a date, serialize as `YYYY-MM-DD` strings, not `Date`/ISO timestamps. Known exception: `issuedOn` on `GET /invoices` still returns a `Date`; it will be migrated separately, so don't change it unless asked, and don't treat it as a pattern to copy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":21676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"371aacbc-94cc-44f6-9faa-afde09b08c81","uuid":"f8a3d17b-1de2-454e-b063-8b119aa52b0f","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:31:42.557Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJmjtnggRLQ7tkJUtrG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015HoHDDgpPS9NdAfJVLrCRY":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.cl